Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:20:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] Return from ICE gathering once the useful candidates
 are in

<details><summary>Claude's draft</summary>

aioice waits on every STUN and TURN request together, so a single interface
whose STUN request never gets an answer (a VPN that drops packets with a
source it does not own, a virtual bridge) holds every connection for the
whole gather timeout, even after the relay and a working server-reflexive
candidate have arrived.

Gathering now returns once the TURN request has finished and one
server-reflexive request has succeeded (or all have finished), after giving
the remaining requests AIORTC_ICE_GATHER_GRACE (default 0.1 s) to answer.
AIORTC_ICE_GATHER_TIMEOUT still caps the whole wait. The rest of
get_component_candidates is aioice 0.10's, unchanged.

Measured against a coturn server from a host with one interface that cannot
reach it, 5 gathers each: 1003-1006 ms before, 195-236 ms after, with the
same candidates (8 host, 1 srflx, 1 relay). The test suite has the same 15
failures before and after, none in ICE.

